
## Frequently Asked Questions

### What Is the Right Age to Start Preschool in India?

Many children start play school between about 2 and 3 years and nursery at around 3. The right age depends on whether your child can manage a few hours away from you. India's National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 considers ages 3 to 6 as the preschool years.

### Is 2 Years Too Early for Preschool?

Not necessarily. Some two-year-olds adjust well to a gentle play school with short sessions, while others need more time. Consider your child's comfort and the quality of the school rather than age alone.

### Is 3 Years the Best Age for Nursery?

Three years is a common age for nursery admission in India and aligns with the preschool stage described in NEP 2020. However, exact age cut-off dates vary by school, so check the latest admission requirements.

### Does Starting Preschool Early Give a Child an Advantage?

Not by itself. Starting early does not guarantee a head start, and starting later is not necessarily a disadvantage. A supportive teacher, a safe environment, and a gentle routine matter more than the starting age.

### What If My Child Cries a Lot at Preschool?

Crying during the first few weeks can be common. Keep goodbyes short and calm, share your child's habits with the teacher, and ask about their daily experience. If distress continues for several weeks, discuss possible changes to the settling-in routine or school environment with the teacher.

### Does My Child Need to Be Toilet Trained Before Preschool?

It depends on the school. Some schools expect children to be toilet trained, while others help them learn. Ask about the school's policy and avoid rushing a child who is not ready.
